   "prompt_tokens": 1596,
   "gen_tokens": 85,
   "gen_s": 35.0,
   "text": "A CPU cache is a small, ultra-fast memory located between the CPU and main RAM that stores frequently accessed data to reduce access latency. When the CPU needs data, it first checks the cache; if found, it retrieves it instantly, but if not, it fetches it from slower main memory. This hierarchy allows the CPU to operate at high speeds without waiting for the much slower RAM to supply every piece of data.<|im_end|>",
